---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, SITE_NAME } from '../../lib/site';
---

<PageLayout
	title="Privacy"
	description="How the International CIN Network website handles personal data and cookies."
>
	<p class="updated">Last updated: 23 October 2026</p>

	<section class="block">
		<h2>Who we are</h2>
		<p>
			This website is run by the {SITE_NAME} (iCIN), an informal, unincorporated network of
			researchers. You can contact us about privacy at{' '}
			<a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="block">
		<h2>What we collect, and why</h2>
		<p>
			We do not ask you to create an account or fill in forms on this site. We collect personal data
			in two ways:
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>Analytics (only if you consent).</strong> If you accept analytics, Cloudflare Web
				Analytics records which pages you visit, how you arrived, your approximate location, and
				your browser and device type. It does not use cookies and does not track you across sites.
				We use this to understand and improve the site. Our legal basis is your consent (Article
				6(1)(a) GDPR).
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Map tiles.</strong> The map on the People page loads its background from OpenFreeMap
				(tiles.openfreemap.org). Your browser sends your IP address to that service to fetch the
				map; see the{' '}
				<a href="https://openfreemap.org/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
					OpenFreeMap privacy policy<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span>
				</a>
				. Our legal basis is our legitimate interest in showing the map (Article 6(1)(f)).
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Hosting.</strong> The site is hosted on GitHub Pages, which logs technical data such
				as IP addresses when pages are requested, to deliver and secure the service.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Emails you send us.</strong> If you write to {CONTACT_EMAIL}, we use your message
				and address only to reply.
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p>Fonts are served from this site, not from a third party.</p>
	</section>

	<section class="block">
		<h2>Cookies and your choices</h2>
		<p>
			This site does not set any cookies. Analytics is off until you accept it. The first time you
			visit, a banner lets you accept or reject it with equal ease. Your choice is saved on your
			device (in local storage, not in a cookie) and we ask again after 12 months.
		</p>
		<p>
			You can change your mind at any time:
			<button type="button" class="linklike" data-consent-open>
				open cookie settings
			</button>
			. If you withdraw consent, analytics stops loading.
		</p>
		<div class="table-wrap">
			<table>
				<caption class="visually-hidden">
					Cookies and similar technologies used on this site
				</caption>
				<thead>
					<tr>
						<th scope="col">Name</th>
						<th scope="col">Provider</th>
						<th scope="col">Purpose</th>
						<th scope="col">Duration</th>
					</tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody>
					<tr>
						<td>icin-consent (local storage)</td>
						<td>This site</td>
						<td>Remembers your cookie choice</td>
						<td>12 months</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td>None</td>
						<td>Cloudflare Web Analytics</td>
						<td>Page-view statistics, without cookies (loaded only with your consent)</td>
						<td>—</td>
					</tr>
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="block">
		<h2>Who receives your data</h2>
		<p>
			Cloudflare, Inc., OpenFreeMap and GitHub, Inc. process data on our behalf or as independent
			providers as described above. Some of them are based in the United States; where that applies,
			transfers rely on the EU–US Data Privacy Framework or standard contractual clauses. We do not
			sell your data.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="block">
		<h2>How long we keep it</h2>
		<p>
			Analytics data is kept only as long as Cloudflare retains data. Server logs are kept by GitHub
			according to its own policy. Emails are kept only as long as needed to answer you.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="block">
		<h2>Your rights</h2>
		<p>
			Under the GDPR you can ask us for access to your personal data, and for it to be corrected,
			erased or restricted. You can object to processing based on legitimate interest, ask for data
			portability, and withdraw consent at any time without affecting earlier processing. Write to{' '}
			<a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. You also have the right to complain
			to your data protection authority.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="block">
		<h2>Changes</h2>
		<p>We will update this page if our practices change, and show the date above.</p>
	</section>
</PageLayout>

<style>
	.updated {
		color: var(--muted);
	}
	ul {
		padding-left: 1.25rem;
	}
	li {
		margin-bottom: 10px;
	}
	.linklike {
		padding: 0;
		font: inherit;
		color: var(--accent);
		background: none;
		border: 0;
		text-decoration: underline;
		text-underline-offset: 3px;
		cursor: pointer;
	}
	.table-wrap {
		overflow-x: auto;
	}
	table {
		width: 100%;
		border-collapse: collapse;
		font-size: 0.9375rem;
	}
	th {
		text-align: left;
		padding: 10px 12px;
		font-size: 0.8125rem;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		color: var(--muted);
		border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ink);
	}
	td {
		padding: 12px;
		vertical-align: top;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
	}
</style>
